Table source provenance
=======================

These files are the inputs used to generate tables/wb86.table and
tables/zm.table.
They are vendored so that release builds do not access the network and the
generated files can be audited and reproduced.  Run
`ruby ../fetch-table-sources.rb` from this directory to retrieve the exact
revisions and verify their SHA-256 digests.

Zhengma
-------

File: zm/zhengma.txt
Upstream: https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5-table-extra
Revision: dbc7154a7f0b9fc04313160ae8066ed4d8cbc446
Original path: tables/zhengma.txt
Imported: 2026-10-04

The upstream README states that its data files are in the public domain.
Debian's licensing audit additionally documents the table family as
clean-room regenerated from the input method's ideas:

https://sources.debian.org/src/fcitx-table-extra/0.3.8-3/debian/README.source/

The upstream statement is preserved as zm/README.

Wubi86
------

File: wb86/wubi-haifeng86.txt
Upstream: https://github.com/mike-fabian/ibus-table-chinese
Revision: 44301450e681c23d60301747856c74b5b9d1312e
Original path: tables/wubi-haifeng/wubi-haifeng86.UTF-8
Imported: 2026-10-04

The BSD 3-clause license added with the table in 2010 is preserved as
wb86/COPYING.  The upstream table header currently labels the table
as 0BSD, but that label does not match the license text and is not used here.

The original 2005 README contains a non-commercial-use statement that appears
to predate the explicit 2010 BSD grant.  It is preserved unmodified as
wb86/README so that this discrepancy remains visible for audit.
